# /game-performance-booster — Per-game performance audit and fixes

This rule triggers the **game-performance-booster** skill. Read `.claude/skills/game-performance-booster/SKILL.md` and follow it strictly.

## What this does

- Takes a **game slug** (e.g. `frogger`, `tetris`) — **one game per session**
- Measures baseline before optimizing (CPU 4×, ~390px viewport, three skins)
- Audits against `performance-checklist.md` and SPEC 11 patterns
- Fixes HUD React, canvas draw/cache, and shared touch CSS when needed
- Target: **≥55 FPS** stable in active play @ CPU 4×
- Updates inventory in `references/game-performance-booster/coverage-log.md`

## What this does NOT do

- Modify landing, library, hall of fame, about, or other non-game pages
- Optimize all playables in one go
- Add FPS overlay to production
- Rewrite engines, permanently lower canvas resolution, or remove skins
- Write specs or mark them as `Aprobado`
- Add E2E FPS tests

## Supporting files

- `.claude/skills/game-performance-booster/SKILL.md` — six-phase workflow and hard rules
- `.claude/skills/game-performance-booster/performance-checklist.md` — per-game audit checklist
- `.claude/skills/game-performance-booster/measurement-protocol.md` — baseline and re-measure steps
- `specs/11-rendimiento-frogger.md` — canonical performance acceptance criteria
- `references/performance-game-patterns.md` — reusable HUD, canvas, touch patterns
- `references/game-performance-booster/coverage-log.md` — performance inventory (read at start, update at end)

## Workflow summary

1. **Context** — read `coverage-log.md`, SPEC 11, patterns, target game files
2. **Confirm game** — single slug from argument or user prompt
3. **Baseline** — measure and document `references/{slug}/performance-baseline.md`
4. **Audit** — walk `performance-checklist.md`
5. **Fix** — minimal diffs in player, render, cache if gaps found
6. **Verify** — re-measure, regression, lint on `/play/{slug}`
7. **Persist** — update game row + append session in `coverage-log.md`, then **STOP**

## Subagent

For a clean context, delegate to [`.cursor/agents/game-performance-booster.md`](.cursor/agents/game-performance-booster.md) when the user explicitly asks for the `@game-performance-booster` subagent.

## Example invocations

```
@game-performance-booster frogger
@game-performance-booster tetris
@game-performance-booster audit
```

## Handoff

After `@spec-impl-game` for a new game → `@game-performance-booster {slug}` after skin-designer and mobile-porter.
